{"full":"hf:GIZ/climate_vulnerability_analysis","spaceId":"GIZ/climate_vulnerability_analysis","name":"Climate Vulnerability Analysis","source":"huggingface","description":"Uncover and summarize vulnerable groups findings","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":2,"created":"2024-10-16T07:54:17.000Z","updated":"2026-05-31T20:04:03.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://giz-climate-vulnerability-analysis.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/GIZ/climate_vulnerability_analysis","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T04:00:03.570Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T04:00:03.570Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T04:00:03.570Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🌡️","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Technical Documentation of the system in accordance with EU AI Act.","Provider / Supplier: GIZ Data Lab & Data Service Center","The Climate Vulnerability App is an AI-powered tool to quickly retrieve and summarize relevant information on marginalised groups from (climate) policy documents, in order to enable users to get a broad overview of the extent to which different marginalised groups are represented in policies. This tool leverages fine-tuned transformer models to classify references related to pre-determined marginalised groups and an LLM of choice to summarize the most important information that has been identified."],"features":["General Description of the System","Model Training Data:","The data used to fine-tune the text classification model can be found here: vulnerabilitytrainingdatafull (will be released soon, in urgent cases please reach out to us via e-mail)","The training data has been collected by human annotators that are expert in their fields","The data does not contain any known bias, however some classes perform better than others (see model card) and risk of potential bias can never be fully excluded."],"sourceUrl":"